Reference: C. Armstrong, L. Thresh, D. Murphy, G. Kearney, "A Perceptual
Evaluation of Individual and Non-Individual HRTFs: A Case Study of the
SADIE II Database", Applied Sciences 8(11), 2029 (2018),
https://doi.org/10.3390/app8112029
Source: https://zenodo.org/records/12092466 (D2_HRIR_SOFA.zip).

Changes: resampled to a 266-direction sphere (nearest measured direction
for each vertex), rotated into the game's listener frame, zero-padded
from 256 to 385 taps, and written in the `hrtf` crate's HRIR format, by
scripts/audio_hrir.py.
